course: dictionary
lesson: 6242
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one is right. The word mode is a good example. «Some apps have a mode for younger users with extra safety» uses mode to mean a setting, a way a machine works.
explain: «Night mode on a phone has not been shown to fix the sleep problem on its own» also uses a setting. Mode can also mean a way or kind of doing something, like a mode of transport. In maths, mode means the value that appears most often in a set of data.
explain: Mode can also mean a state of mind. «Fear sends your body into alarm mode» means your body is in a state of high alert. Ask yourself what the sentence is about: travel, a machine, numbers or feelings? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Mode has several meanings, so check the context to find the right one.
fact: A mode of transport is a way of travelling, such as bus, car, bike or walking.
fact: A mode on a machine is a setting, such as silent mode or airplane mode.
fact: In maths, the mode is the value that appears most often in a set of data.
fact: Informally, a mode can be a mood, as in panic mode or holiday mode.
exercise: Sam goes to school by bike, so his mode of transport is a bike. What does mode mean here? | A mood or feeling | The most common number | Way of travelling | *A way of travelling | A setting on a machine
exercise: «Put your phone on silent mode.» What does mode mean here? | A way of travelling | A kind of fruit | *A setting that makes the phone work in a particular way | A number that appears most
exercise: In the numbers 2, 5, 5, 7, 5, 9, which value is the mode? | 7 | 2 | *5 | 9
test: «Fear sends your body into alarm mode: fast heart, tight muscles.» What does alarm mode suggest? | Holiday fun | A quiet setting | A way of travelling | *A state of being on high alert
test: In the numbers 4, 6, 6, 8, 10, which value is the mode? | *6 | 4 | 10 | 8
exam: Ruby says «night mode» on a phone means she is sleepy. Which meaning of mode is right? | A mood or state of mind | A way of travelling | The most common value in a set | *A setting that makes the phone work in a particular way
